l,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in: 4.5.1.stable, v4.6.dev.custom_build [c5f207fdc]\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.6.dev (c5f207fdc) - Arch Linux #1 SMP PREEMPT_DYNAMIC Mon, 24 Nov 2025 15:21:09 +0000 on X11 - X11 display driver, Multi-window, 2 monitors - OpenGL 3 (Compatibility) - NVIDIA GeForce RTX 3060 Ti (nvidia; 580.105.08) - 13th Gen Intel(R) Core(TM) i5-13400F (16 threads) - 15.37 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nIn the project manager, a project can have its list of tags displayed.\n\nThe list of tags did not include any mechanism for overflow handling, so the side bar will simply be pushed out of boundary when the list of tags is too wide.\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/0e2052dc-0b61-4892-89d1-76b001a92a4b)\n\nThis is probably not a very big deal for desktop users. But for mobile users, the screen size can't be changed :(\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Open the Project Manager\n2. Make sure there is at least one project in the list\n3. Select one project and click Manage Tags\n4. Add some tags so that the list of tags becomes very wide\n5. Check that the side bar is pushed out of the boundary\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nN/A","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","